{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And you shall refrain from leaving to him.</b> Refrain — and beware of being one who leaves it collapsed under its load; rather, you shall surely help leave it with him, as its Targum: 'you shall surely leave with him what is in your heart upon it, and you shall unload with him.' This is hinted at in Rashi's commentary in parashat Re'eh, regarding the inciter." "<b>You shall help with him.</b> As stated in Bava Metzia: the owner of the donkey should not go and sit idle and say, 'Since the commandment is upon you, if you wish to unload — unload.' Therefore <b>with him</b> is stated — if he leaves it [unloaded], you are permitted to leave it." "<b>With him.</b> It is impossible to unload a beast's burden except with two people — one unloading from this side and one unloading from the other side."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:58.839330025Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}